'' 'this = x' ASSIGNS THE OBJECT. 'this' is held as the pointer the ABI passes, so a value of
'' another type read as a pointer assignment: TKO0670 for a double ("a pointer and a
'' floating-point value do not convert"), and for a longint only TKO0830 -- after which the
'' value was stored over the pointer, and the object never changed. fbc calls the matching
'' 'operator let' for both and prints 2.5 and 3.5 (fbc-modern 1.20, 2026-09-29).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/this-assign-let.bas -o tests/driver/thisassignlet.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/driver/thisassignlet.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  2.5 3.5
